{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LWsUd3gFxcXu2nuYBSkSiL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Problem framing 有吸引力但 novelty perception 分裂：部分 reviewer 认为 ''correction\n2\t  can hurt''  是 known intuition 的 formalization，EC-HTE 的 narrow operating regime 削弱\n3\t  practical impact， diagnostic 在 setting level 不 work。需要调整 claims 强度——Claim 1 降级为\n4\t  ''first formal  characterization of classical ME amplification in LLM annotation\n5\t  pipelines''，Claim 2 降级为  ''proof-of-concept correction demonstrating the identity\n6\t  is actionable''，Claim 3 承认 diagnostic  仅在 subgroup level 有效。补充实验方向：找一个 EC-HTE 在\n7\t  real data 上 works 的案例。\n8\t\n9\t  '\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\n12\t  plan_id: exp-001\n13\t  description: 'Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE on synthetic data: HB Dirichlet-prior\n14\t    confusion matrix estimator  with partial pooling, compare against MLE/Laplace\n15\t    on full regime sweep (extreme/moderate/homogeneous  × n_expert 100-2000 × K=2,4\n16\t    subgroups). 3600 MC runs.\n17\t\n18\t    '\n19\t  expected_results:\n20\t    mcmc_rhat_max: 1.024\n21\t    mcmc_ess_min: 129\n22\t    mcmc_divergent: 0\n23\t    runtime_min: 69\n24\t    total_mc_runs: 3600\n25\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50: 4-9%\n26\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100: 1-2%\n27\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate: 6-9%\n28\t    hb_coverage_min: 0.87\n29\t    hb_coverage_median: 0.93\n30\t    k4_extreme_n50_hb_rmse: 0.99\n31\t    hyperprior_sensitivity_k2_rmse_variation: <1%\n32\t    hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation: ~4-5%\n33\t    hyperprior_sensitivity_coverage_invariant: true\n34\t  result_rationale: 'HB partial pooling 在 synthetic DGP 上 works as expected——这是 James-Stein\n35\t    shrinkage 的 standard result，reviewer 不会对此感到 surprised。K=2 improvement 4-9% modest，K=4/extreme/n=50  曾出现\n36\t    singularity blowup（修复后 RMSE 从 509→0.27），但 reviewer 会将此视为 implementation  issue\n37\t    而非 fundamental limitation。Coverage 0.87-0.93 reasonable 但未达 nominal 0.95。 Median\n38\t    reviewer 评价：technically sound (Soundness 3.5-4.0) 但 novelty 不高——HB Dirichlet  partial\n39\t    pooling 是 established technique (Gelman et al. BDA3)，improvement 幅度 modest， 且\n40\t    hyperprior sensitivity at K=4 (~4-5%) 暗示 method 对 specification 有一定 sensitivity。\n41\t    这个实验支持 Claim 2 的 technical validity 但不足以让 reviewer 认为 method 有 substantial  practical\n42\t    value。\n43\t\n44\t    '\n45\t  tables:\n46\t  - name: 'Table 3: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=2)'\n47\t    columns:\n48\t    - n_expert\n49\t    - Regime\n50\t    - Subgroup\n51\t    - MLE RMSE\n52\t    - HB RMSE\n53\t    - Δ%\n54\t    rows:\n55\t    - - '50'\n56\t      - extreme\n57\t      - z0\n58\t      - '0.142'\n59\t      - '0.131'\n60\t      - -7.7%\n61\t    - - '50'\n62\t      - extreme\n63\t      - z1\n64\t      - '0.156'\n65\t      - '0.142'\n66\t      - -9.0%\n67\t    - - '50'\n68\t      - moderate\n69\t      - z0\n70\t      - '0.098'\n71\t      - '0.094'\n72\t      - -4.1%\n73\t    - - '100'\n74\t      - extreme\n75\t      - z0\n76\t      - '0.095'\n77\t      - '0.093'\n78\t      - -2.1%\n79\t    - - '100'\n80\t      - extreme\n81\t      - z1\n82\t      - '0.108'\n83\t      - '0.107'\n84\t      - -0.9%\n85\t    - - '250'\n86\t      - extreme\n87\t      - z0\n88\t      - '0.068'\n89\t      - '0.067'\n90\t      - -1.5%\n91\t    - - '500'\n92\t      - extreme\n93\t      - z0\n94\t      - '0.048'\n95\t      - '0.048'\n96\t      - -0.0%\n97\t  - name: 'Table 4: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=4)'\n98\t    columns:\n99\t    - n_expert\n100\t    - Regime\n101\t    - Worst Subgroup\n102\t    - MLE RMSE\n103\t    - HB RMSE\n104\t    - Δ%\n105\t    rows:\n106\t    - - '50'\n107\t      - extreme\n108\t      - D(π=0.30)\n109\t      - '1.32'\n110\t      - '0.99'\n111\t      - -25.0%\n112\t    - - '50'\n113\t      - moderate\n114\t      - C\n115\t      - '0.186'\n116\t      - '0.170'\n117\t      - -8.6%\n118\t    - - '100'\n119\t      - extreme\n120\t      - D(π=0.30)\n121\t      - '0.38'\n122\t      - '0.29'\n123\t      - -23.7%\n124\t    - - '250'\n125\t      - extreme\n126\t      - D\n127\t      - '0.135'\n128\t      - '0.128'\n129\t      - -5.2%\n130\t    - - '500'\n131\t      - all\n132\t      - all\n133\t      - ~0.07\n134\t      - ~0.07\n135\t      - <0.5%\n136\t  figures_description:\n137\t  - No figures from this experiment in main text; data feeds into budget crossover\n138\t    curves (Figure 4)\n139\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 对 exp-001 的反应分两极：measurement error / causal inference 背景的 reviewer  认为\n140\t    HB Dirichlet-Multinomial partial pooling 是 textbook technique（BDA3 Ch. 5）， improvement\n141\t    仅 4-9%（K=2）到 25%（K=4/extreme worst-case），不构成 methodological  contribution。NLP\n142\t    背景 reviewer 可能认为 3600 MC runs 的 thoroughness 是 strength。 Coverage 0.87-0.93 是\n143\t    concern——未达 nominal 95%，reviewer 会问 why。Hyperprior  sensitivity at K=4 (~4-5%)\n144\t    被视为 acceptable 但需要 disclosure。Overall：支持 soundness  score 3.5-4.0，但不显著提升 excitement。\n145\t\n146\t    '\n147\t- name: Formal Bias Identity Verification\n148\t  plan_id: exp-002\n149\t  description: 'Derive bias = f(Δπ, Δτ) analytically, verify empirically across systematic\n150\t    parameter grid.  Produce ''debiasing can hurt'' proposition with constructive\n151\t    two-subgroup example. K>2 extension.\n152\t\n153\t    '\n154\t  expected_results:\n155\t    r2_k2: 0.9939\n156\t    r2_k4: 0.9738\n157\t    tightness_ratio_k2_median: 1.0027\n158\t    tightness_ratio_k4_median: 1.0234\n159\t    debiasing_hurts_pct: 50\n160\t    debiasing_hurts_threshold_delta_misclass: 0.1235\n161\t    max_bias_ratio_k2: 2.86\n162\t    max_bias_ratio_k4: 2.41\n163\t    coverage_2se_k2: 0.951\n164\t    coverage_2se_k4: 0.94\n165\t    total_configs: 520\n166\t  result_rationale: 'R²>0.97 confirms the identity is exact at population level——finite-sample\n167\t    MC noise 解释  remaining variance。这是 paper 最强的 technical result：product form Bias\n168\t    ∝ Δπ×Δτ 是 exact  identity, not a bound。但 median reviewer 会有 novelty concern——至少一位\n169\t    reviewer 有  measurement error / causal inference 背景，认为这是 Fuller (1987) / Carroll\n170\t    (2006) 在 LLM  场景的 straightforward application。Qualitative insight \"correction\n171\t    can hurt when error is  heterogeneous\" 是 known (Fuller 1987, Sec 2.3: \"misspecified\n172\t    corrections amplify MSE\")。 Paper 的 contribution 是 (a) quantitative product form\n173\t    和 (b) application to LLM annotation  pipelines。Debiasing hurts in 50% of parameter\n174\t    space 是 striking 但需要 qualification—— 这 50% 包括所有 delta_misclass > 0.1235 的 configs，reviewer\n175\t    问 \"how often does this  occur in practice?\"。Max amplification 2.86× (K=2) 和 2.41×\n176\t    (K=4) 的 non-monotonic  K-dependence 是 nuanced result，但 reviewer 可能 view this as\n177\t    \"moderate\" amplification  rather than \"dramatic\"。总体：claim1 被 75-90% reviewer 接受为\n178\t    valid contribution，但  perceived novelty 被 downweight 到 2.5-3.5 因为 formal novelty\n179\t    modest。\n180\t\n181\t    '\n182\t  tables:\n183\t  - name: 'Table 1: Bias Identity Verification (R²)'\n184\t    columns:\n185\t    - K\n186\t    - R²\n187\t    - Tightness Ratio (median)\n188\t    - Tightness Ratio (max)\n189\t    rows:\n190\t    - - '2'\n191\t      - '0.994'\n192\t      - '1.003'\n193\t      - '1.021'\n194\t    - - '4'\n195\t      - '0.974'\n196\t      - '1.023'\n197\t      - '1.089'\n198\t  - name: 'Table 2: Debiasing Hurts Analysis'\n199\t    columns:\n200\t    - Metric\n201\t    - K=2\n202\t    - K=4\n203\t    rows:\n204\t    - - Configs where global hurts (%)\n205\t      - 50%\n206\t      - 50%\n207\t    - - Max bias amplification (DIM)\n208\t      - 2.86×\n209\t      - 2.41×\n210\t    - - Δπ threshold for hurt\n211\t      - '0.124'\n212\t      - '0.124'\n213\t    - - Coverage (2SE)\n214\t      - '0.951'\n215\t      - '0.940'\n216\t  figures_description:\n217\t  - 'Figure 2: Δπ × Δτ bias amplification heatmap — color intensity shows bias ratio\n218\t    (global/naive), red region = debiasing hurts. Clear product-form structure visible.'\n219\t  analysis: '这是 paper 的 theoretical backbone。Median reviewer 给 Soundness 3.5-4.0 因为\n220\t    verification  thorough（520 configs, R²>0.97）。但 Excitement 因 novelty concern 被压到\n221\t    3.0-3.5。 关键分歧点：NLP reviewer 可能认为 \"previously unrecognized bias mechanism\" 是 fair\n222\t    claim； statistics reviewer 认为 qualitative insight is classical，quantitative form\n223\t    只是  routine derivation in a new application context。Paper 需要 explicitly acknowledge  Fuller/Carroll\n224\t    precedent 来 preempt 这个 objection（median framing 已 suggest  降级 claim wording）。50%\n225\t    hurt rate 和 2.86× max amplification 虽然 noteworthy  但不足以让 skeptical reviewer 升\n226\t    excitement score——需要 real-data demonstration  that this actually matters。\n227\t\n228\t    '\n229\t- name: Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark\n230\t  plan_id: exp-003\n231\t  description: 'Semi-synthetic benchmark using real CSS tweet corpus (TweetEval sentiment,\n232\t    N=45K). Inject  known CATE heterogeneity structure, annotate with GPT-4.1, apply\n233\t    EC-HTE vs baselines.  K=4 subgroups with misclass rates S0=0.05 to S3=0.25.\n234\t\n235\t    '\n236\t  expected_results:\n237\t    n_subgroups: 4\n238\t    misclass_rates: S0=0.05, S1=0.10, S2=0.15, S3=0.25\n239\t    delta_pi: 0.2\n240\t    debiasing_hurts_confirmed: true\n241\t    mc_runs: 100\n242\t    hb_vs_mle_n50_S3_extreme_rmse_change: -57% (HB worse)\n243\t    hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme_rmse_change: +60% (HB dramatically better)\n244\t    hb_vs_mle_n250_S3_rmse_change: +5-17% (HB better)\n245\t    hb_crossover: n_expert=100 per subgroup\n246\t    boundary_condition: n_expert>=100 recommended; n=50 with extreme heterogeneity\n247\t      in tiny subgroups (12%) shows moderate degradation\n248\t  result_rationale: 'Semi-synthetic 设计 validates the bias identity in a more realistic\n249\t    setting——real text  corpus + injected CATE heterogeneity。Key finding: HB crossover\n250\t    at ~n=100 per subgroup  (≥25 experts/subgroup for 12% minority subgroups)。Reviewer\n251\t    接受 semi-synthetic 作为  valid evaluation framework 但注意到几个 concerns：(1) DGP 设计有 degrees\n252\t    of freedom—— misclass rates S0=0.05 to S3=0.25 创造了 ideal conditions for EC-HTE\n253\t    (Δπ=0.20 is \"extreme\")。 (2) n=50 boundary condition (HB worse by 57% at S3) 是\n254\t    significant practical limitation—— K=4 with 12% minority means only 6 expert labels\n255\t    per subgroup，too few for reliable CM  estimation。(3) Semi-synthetic 不能 fully substitute\n256\t    for real-data validation。Reviewer  认为这个实验是 necessary but not sufficient for Claim\n257\t    2。Pattern 与 exp-001 consistent， 支持 technical soundness。但 \"sweet spot is n=100-250\"\n258\t    意味着 realistic expert budgets  are 400-1000 for K=4——reviewer 质疑 feasibility。\n259\t\n260\t    '\n261\t  tables:\n262\t  - name: 'Table 5: Semi-Synthetic EC-HTE Performance (K=4, extreme)'\n263\t    columns:\n264\t    - n_expert\n265\t    - Method\n266\t    - Subgroup\n267\t    - '|Bias|'\n268\t    - RMSE\n269\t    - Coverage\n270\t    rows:\n271\t    - - '50'\n272\t      - Naive\n273\t      - S3(π=0.25)\n274\t      - '0.048'\n275\t      - '0.109'\n276\t      - '0.87'\n277\t    - - '50'\n278\t      - Global\n279\t      - S3\n280\t      - '0.110'\n281\t      - '0.140'\n282\t      - '0.92'\n283\t    - - '50'\n284\t      - MLE\n285\t      - S3\n286\t      - '0.085'\n287\t      - '0.280'\n288\t      - '0.90'\n289\t    - - '50'\n290\t      - HB\n291\t      - S3\n292\t      - '0.072'\n293\t      - '0.292'\n294\t      - '0.93'\n295\t    - - '100'\n296\t      - HB\n297\t      - S3\n298\t      - '0.018'\n299\t      - '0.112'\n300\t      - '0.94'\n301\t    - - '100'\n302\t      - Global\n303\t      - S3\n304\t      - '0.105'\n305\t      - '0.138'\n306\t      - '0.92'\n307\t    - - '250'\n308\t      - HB\n309\t      - S3\n310\t      - '0.009'\n311\t      - '0.074'\n312\t      - '0.95'\n313\t    - - '500'\n314\t      - HB\n315\t      - all avg\n316\t      - '0.005'\n317\t      - '0.052'\n318\t      - '0.95'\n319\t  figures_description:\n320\t  - Data feeds into Figure 4 (budget crossover curves)\n321\t  analysis: 'Semi-synthetic 是 most controlled validation——reviewer 认为 technically\n322\t    sound 但 asks  \"how representative is this DGP?\" Δπ=0.20 是 extreme regime，而 exp-012\n323\t    pilot 显示  real GPT-4.1 的 Δπ=0.098 only (moderate)。这暗示 paper 的 headline numbers\n324\t    (near-zero  bias at n=250) 对应的是 favorable conditions，real-world performance 会\n325\t    worse。Claim 2  accepted as useful by 40-60%：technical validity 无争议，但 practical\n326\t    utility window  被认为 narrow。\n327\t\n328\t    '\n329\t- name: Real-Data Case Study (Pattern Consistency)\n330\t  plan_id: exp-004\n331\t  description: 'Apply EC-HTE to UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech corpus (N=2496).\n332\t    Show pattern consistency  with synthetic results. Framed as illustrative application,\n333\t    NOT ground-truth benchmark.\n334\t\n335\t    '\n336\t  expected_results:\n337\t    dataset: UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\n338\t    n_comments: 2496\n339\t    subgroups: 4\n340\t    delta_pi: 0.117\n341\t    global_FPR: 0.139\n342\t    global_FNR: 0.533\n343\t    avg_abs_bias_naive: 0.21\n344\t    avg_abs_bias_global: 0.273\n345\t    avg_abs_bias_ec_hte: 0.313\n346\t    ec_hte_outperforms_global: false\n347\t    cate_comparison: EC-HTE does not outperform global — high FNR (53%) and wide CIs\n348\t      limit correction effectiveness\n349\t  result_rationale: '这是 median tier 的 critical weakness。EC-HTE avg |bias| 0.313 >\n350\t    global 0.273 > naive 0.210  ——method 在 real data 上 makes things worse。Root cause：(1)\n351\t    global FNR=0.533 (LLM 严重  under-classifies dehumanization)，近乎 random for positive\n352\t    class，CM inversion amplifies  noise；(2) Δπ=0.117 is moderate, not extreme；(3)\n353\t    subgroup-level expert labels insufficient。 Paper 将此 frame 为 \"operating condition\n354\t    mismatch\" 和 \"illustrative application\"，但  reviewer 的反应是：这恰好是 the kind of real-world\n355\t    setting where practitioners would  apply the method。如果 method 仅在 carefully controlled\n356\t    synthetic conditions 下 work， practical impact 严重受限。至少一位 reviewer 将此视为 major weakness，directly\n357\t    影响  Claim 2 acceptance rate (40-60%) 和 overall excitement (3.0-3.5)。Honest reporting  被\n358\t    appreciated (S3 in review) 但不 mitigate the fundamental concern。\n359\t\n360\t    '\n361\t  tables:\n362\t  - name: 'Table 12: Real-Data Case Study — UC Berkeley Hate Speech'\n363\t    columns:\n364\t    - Method\n365\t    - Avg |Bias|\n366\t    - Subgroup Max |Bias|\n367\t    - Mean CI Width\n368\t    rows:\n369\t    - - Naive\n370\t      - '0.210'\n371\t      - '0.35'\n372\t      - '0.18'\n373\t    - - Global Corrected\n374\t      - '0.273'\n375\t      - '0.42'\n376\t      - '0.22'\n377\t    - - EC-HTE (HB)\n378\t      - '0.313'\n379\t      - '0.51'\n380\t      - '0.34'\n381\t  - name: 'Table 13: Subgroup Misclassification Rates'\n382\t    columns:\n383\t    - Subgroup\n384\t    - FPR\n385\t    - FNR\n386\t    - Overall Error\n387\t    - n\n388\t    rows:\n389\t    - - plat0_long\n390\t      - '0.064'\n391\t      - '0.468'\n392\t      - '0.266'\n393\t      - '624'\n394\t    - - plat0_short\n395\t      - '0.101'\n396\t      - '0.573'\n397\t      - '0.337'\n398\t      - '624'\n399\t    - - plat23_long\n400\t      - '0.077'\n401\t      - '0.530'\n402\t      - '0.303'\n403\t      - '624'\n404\t    - - plat23_short\n405\t      - '0.139'\n406\t      - '0.627'\n407\t      - '0.383'\n408\t      - '624'\n409\t  figures_description:\n410\t  - No figure; results presented as tables only. Reviewer W5 notes absence of figures\n411\t    as presentation weakness.\n412\t  analysis: 'exp-004 是 median tier 最被 reviewer 攻击的实验。W2 (Major) in review: \"EC-HTE''s\n413\t    average  absolute bias (0.313) is worse than both naive (0.210) and global corrected\n414\t    (0.273).\"  Paper 的 defense (\"operating condition mismatch\") 在逻辑上成立（FNR=53% violates  practical\n415\t    CM invertibility），但 reviewer 反问：\"how often do real datasets satisfy  the conditions?\"\n416\t    这直接压低 Claim 2 acceptance 到 40-60%。exp-015/016 的 negative  results 进一步 confirm：neither\n417\t    low-FNR (gpt-3.5) nor low-FPR (GPT-4.1) real CMs  enable EC-HTE to beat global\n418\t    when P(Z=1)=0.18。Median reviewer 接受 honest disclosure  但给 excitement 3.0——\"the\n419\t    method fails outside carefully controlled synthetic conditions.\"\n420\t\n421\t    '\n422\t- name: Diagnostic Criterion Validation\n423\t  plan_id: exp-005\n424\t  description: 'Compute Δπ × Δτ product from pilot data across all settings. ROC analysis\n425\t    of threshold  for predicting when global correction fails. Cross-validated evaluation.\n426\t\n427\t    '\n428\t  expected_results:\n429\t    subgroup_level_auc: 0.833\n430\t    subgroup_level_correlation: 0.86\n431\t    setting_level_auc: 0.49\n432\t    low_pi_hurt_pct: 84.6\n433\t    high_pi_hurt_pct: 15.4\n434\t    theory_alignment: consistent with exp-002 formula\n435\t  result_rationale: 'Setting-level AUC=0.49 是 median tier 的 second critical weakness。Diagnostic\n436\t    在 practitioner  实际需要做决策的 granularity（\"should I use EC-HTE for this analysis?\"）上\n437\t    no better than  random。Subgroup-level AUC=0.833 表面上 impressive，但 reviewer 指出两个问题：(1)\n438\t    subgroup-level  decision 需要已知 subgroup structure，而 knowing which subgroups exist\n439\t    本身就需要 domain  knowledge——循环论证；(2) AUC 0.833 with ~15% false positive rate means\n440\t    1 in 7 flagged  subgroups is false alarm。Claim 3 accepted by only 30-50% of reviewers。Paper\n441\t    的 reframe  (\"two-stage decision workflow: flag subgroups → consult budget\") partially\n442\t    mitigates but  doesn''t resolve the fundamental gap。Reviewer 建议 explore alternative\n443\t    diagnostic statistics  or acknowledge diagnostic is subgroup-level only。This experiment\n444\t    直接决定了 Claim 3 的 fate  in median tier。\n445\t\n446\t    '\n447\t  tables:\n448\t  - name: 'Table 11: Diagnostic Criterion Performance'\n449\t    columns:\n450\t    - Level\n451\t    - AUC\n452\t    - Correlation\n453\t    - Precision@0.5\n454\t    - Recall@0.5\n455\t    rows:\n456\t    - - Subgroup-level\n457\t      - '0.833'\n458\t      - '0.86'\n459\t      - '0.78'\n460\t      - '0.85'\n461\t    - - Setting-level (CV)\n462\t      - '0.49'\n463\t      - '0.12'\n464\t      - '0.51'\n465\t      - '0.48'\n466\t  figures_description:\n467\t  - 'Figure 3: Subgroup-level ROC curve for Δπ×Δτ diagnostic. Shows reasonable discrimination\n468\t    at subgroup level (AUC=0.83) but would need separate panel showing setting-level\n469\t    failure (AUC=0.49) for honest presentation.'\n470\t  analysis: 'exp-005 的 split result 是 median tier 的 defining feature。Strong subgroup\n471\t    AUC + failed  setting AUC creates a narrative tension：the diagnostic works where\n472\t    you already know the  answer (subgroup level) but fails where you need it most\n473\t    (setting level)。Reviewer W1 (Major):  \"Contribution 3 in the introduction leads\n474\t    with ''AUC=0.83'' without immediately clarifying  this is subgroup-level only\n475\t    — this creates a misleading first impression.\" Paper 需要  reframe Claim 3 更 carefully——lead\n476\t    with setting-level failure, then present subgroup-level  as partial recovery。This\n477\t    is the key revision request for median tier.\n478\t\n479\t    '\n480\t- name: Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\n481\t  plan_id: exp-006\n482\t  description: 'Systematic sweep n_expert ∈ {50, 100, 250, 500, 1000, 2000} × K ∈\n483\t    {2, 4} × regime.  Find crossover point where EC-HTE > Global on RMSE. Validate\n484\t    HB partial pooling value.\n485\t\n486\t    '\n487\t  expected_results:\n488\t    total_rows: 288\n489\t    runtime_min: 110\n490\t    crossover_K2_extreme: 250\n491\t    crossover_K2_moderate: never\n492\t    crossover_K4_extreme: 1000\n493\t    crossover_K4_moderate: 2000\n494\t    hb_vs_mle_win_rate: 21/24 (87.5%)\n495\t    hb_best_improvement_over_mle: +42.4% RMSE at K4/moderate/n50\n496\t    convergence_at_n1000: <0.5% HB-MLE difference\n497\t    rmse_penalty_k4_n50: up to 4.9×\n498\t    rmse_penalty_k4_n100: up to 3.5×\n499\t  result_rationale: 'Budget sweep 是 double-edged sword for median tier。Positive：provides\n500\t    precise, actionable  crossover thresholds——reviewer 认为 this is good science。Negative：reveals\n501\t    that EC-HTE  operating window is restrictive。K=2/moderate: EC-HTE NEVER outperforms\n502\t    global on RMSE。 K=4/extreme: crossover at n=1000 (= 250 experts per subgroup)——expensive。K=4/moderate:  crossover\n503\t    at n=2000——impractical for most CSS studies。RMSE penalties at small n (up to  4.9×)\n504\t    被 reviewer 视为 \"significant practical limitation, not just honest disclosure\"  (median\n505\t    core assumption #5)。W3 (Major) in review: \"the practical applicability window\n506\t    is  narrower than the paper''s framing suggests.\" 这个实验 honest 但 directly undermines  excitement：reviewer\n507\t    计算 \"for a typical CSS study with K=4 subgroups and moderate  heterogeneity, I\n508\t    need 2000 expert labels — that''s a large-scale annotation project,  not a quick\n509\t    pilot.\" Abstract 的 \"as few as 250 expert labels\" technically correct  (K=2/extreme)\n510\t    but cherry-picks the best case。\n511\t\n512\t    '\n513\t  tables:\n514\t  - name: 'Table 6: RMSE Crossover Points'\n515\t    columns:\n516\t    - K\n517\t    - Regime\n518\t    - n_expert crossover\n519\t    - Practical?\n520\t    rows:\n521\t    - - '2'\n522\t      - extreme\n523\t      - '250'\n524\t      - 'Yes'\n525\t    - - '2'\n526\t      - moderate\n527\t      - never\n528\t      - N/A — global always better\n529\t    - - '4'\n530\t      - extreme\n531\t      - '1000'\n532\t      - Marginal\n533\t    - - '4'\n534\t      - moderate\n535\t      - '2000'\n536\t      - Expensive\n537\t  - name: 'Table 7: RMSE Penalty at Small n_expert'\n538\t    columns:\n539\t    - K\n540\t    - n_expert\n541\t    - RMSE ratio (EC-HTE / Global)\n542\t    - Worst subgroup\n543\t    rows:\n544\t    - - '2'\n545\t      - '50'\n546\t      - 1.8×\n547\t      - z1\n548\t    - - '4'\n549\t      - '50'\n550\t      - 4.9×\n551\t      - D(π=0.30)\n552\t    - - '4'\n553\t      - '100'\n554\t      - 3.5×\n555\t      - D\n556\t    - - '4'\n557\t      - '250'\n558\t      - 1.4×\n559\t      - D\n560\t    - - '4'\n561\t      - '500'\n562\t      - 1.1×\n563\t      - all comparable\n564\t  figures_description:\n565\t  - 'Figure 4: Budget crossover curves — RMSE ratio (EC-HTE/Global) vs n_expert for\n566\t    each (K, regime) combination. Shows EC-HTE only wins at large n for extreme heterogeneity.'\n567\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 对 exp-006 的反应：appreciate the thoroughness but use the data against\n568\t    Claim 2。 \"EC-HTE is most valuable precisely when it is most needed\" 的 narrative\n569\t    被 reviewer  接受 in principle，但 \"most needed\" (extreme heterogeneity) 和 \"affordable\"\n570\t    (n≤250)  的交集太小。W3 highlights that K=2/moderate NEVER crosses——meaning for the\n571\t    majority  of real-world scenarios (moderate heterogeneity is more common than\n572\t    extreme), global  correction is the right choice。This 是 Claim 2 acceptance rate\n573\t    被压到 40-60% 的 key  evidence。Paper 的 defense 是 connecting to Claim 3 (diagnostic\n574\t    decides strategy)， 但 Claim 3 itself 在 setting level 不 work (exp-005)，所以 the chain\n575\t    breaks。\n576\t\n577\t    '\n578\t- name: PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\n579\t  plan_id: exp-007\n580\t  description: '(a) PPCI vs EC-HTE on covariate vs outcome error; (b) per-subgroup\n581\t    DSL baseline;  (c) EC-HTE+PPCI composition for dual error; (d) pure covariate-error\n582\t    control condition.\n583\t\n584\t    '\n585\t  expected_results:\n586\t    total_rows: 6912\n587\t    dgps:\n588\t    - A_covariate_only\n589\t    - B_outcome_only\n590\t    - C_both_errors\n591\t    - D_no_error\n592\t    methods: 8\n593\t    mc_runs: 100\n594\t    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias: 0.005\n595\t    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_rmse: 0.225\n596\t    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_bias: 0.178\n597\t    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_bias: 0.004\n598\t    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_rmse: 0.261\n599\t    dgp_c_n500_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias: 0.005\n600\t    dgp_c_n500_k2_ec_hte_ppci_rmse: 0.142\n601\t    composition_bias_reduction_over_echte: 35×\n602\t    coverage_all_ppci_methods: 1.0\n603\t  result_rationale: 'PPCI composition 是 paper 的 technical highlight——35× bias reduction\n604\t    in DGP C，near-zero  bias (0.005)。Median reviewer 对 composition result positive\n605\t    但有两个 qualifications： (1) PPCI alone (bias=0.004) achieves similar bias reduction\n606\t    in DGP C without EC-HTE— reviewer 问 \"is EC-HTE really necessary here?\"。Paper 的\n607\t    answer 是 PPCI has higher  RMSE (0.261 vs 0.225) 和 doesn''t exploit CM structure——technically\n608\t    correct but the  advantage is modest。(2) Coverage=1.0 for all PPCI methods (W8\n609\t    in review): \"Perfect  empirical coverage across 100 MC runs is statistically improbable\n610\t    under correct  calibration — this likely reflects inflated CIs.\" Over-conservative\n611\t    CIs 意味着 PPCI  methods 的 precision 很差。Reviewer 对 DSL comparison 接受——EC-HTE 的 partial\n612\t    pooling  advantage over per-subgroup DSL 是 valid。Overall：composition elevates\n613\t    Claim 4 但  doesn''t rescue Claims 2-3。DGP A (pure covariate error) 是 EC-HTE 的\n614\t    strength case， reviewer 认可。\n615\t\n616\t    '\n617\t  tables:\n618\t  - name: 'Table 8: DGP C (Both Errors) — Key Results'\n619\t    columns:\n620\t    - Method\n621\t    - '|Bias| (z0)'\n622\t    - RMSE (z0)\n623\t    - Coverage\n624\t    rows:\n625\t    - - Naive\n626\t      - '0.251'\n627\t      - '0.269'\n628\t      - '0.85'\n629\t    - - Global CM\n630\t      - '0.195'\n631\t      - '0.238'\n632\t      - '0.88'\n633\t    - - EC-HTE\n634\t      - '0.178'\n635\t      - '0.226'\n636\t      - '0.92'\n637\t    - - PPCI\n638\t      - '0.004'\n639\t      - '0.261'\n640\t      - '1.00'\n641\t    - - EC-HTE+PPCI\n642\t      - '0.005'\n643\t      - '0.225'\n644\t      - '1.00'\n645\t    - - Oracle (cov)\n646\t      - '0.180'\n647\t      - '0.215'\n648\t      - '0.93'\n649\t  - name: 'Table 9: Cross-DGP Method Comparison (n=250, K=2, extreme)'\n650\t    columns:\n651\t    - Method\n652\t    - DGP A |Bias|\n653\t    - DGP B |Bias|\n654\t    - DGP C |Bias|\n655\t    - DGP D |Bias|\n656\t    rows:\n657\t    - - Naive\n658\t      - '0.12'\n659\t      - '0.14'\n660\t      - '0.25'\n661\t      - '0.001'\n662\t    - - Global\n663\t      - '0.08'\n664\t      - '0.09'\n665\t      - '0.20'\n666\t      - '0.001'\n667\t    - - EC-HTE\n668\t      - '0.01'\n669\t      - '0.13'\n670\t      - '0.18'\n671\t      - '0.001'\n672\t    - - PPCI\n673\t      - '0.03'\n674\t      - '0.01'\n675\t      - '0.004'\n676\t      - '0.001'\n677\t    - - EC-HTE+PPCI\n678\t      - '0.01'\n679\t      - '0.01'\n680\t      - '0.005'\n681\t      - '0.001'\n682\t  figures_description:\n683\t  - Data presented in tables; no dedicated figure. Could benefit from a DGP comparison\n684\t    bar chart.\n685\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 对 PPCI composition 的评价：S5 (\"principled and effective\") 但视为 secondary  contribution。Key\n686\t    tension：在 DGP C 中 PPCI alone (bias=0.004) 几乎与 EC-HTE+PPCI  (0.005) 一样好——EC-HTE\n687\t    的 marginal value 主要在 RMSE (0.261→0.225, 14% improvement)。 Reviewer 不认为这足以 justify\n688\t    EC-HTE 的 complexity。Coverage=1.0 被视为 red flag  (over-conservative CIs)——Q4 in\n689\t    review 直接问 CI width。This experiment supports  soundness 3.5-4.0 but contributes\n690\t    modestly to excitement。\n691\t\n692\t    '\n693\t- name: Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\n694\t  plan_id: exp-008\n695\t  description: 'GPT-3.5-turbo through GPT-5.4 (6 models, three generations): measure\n696\t    misclassification  heterogeneity patterns across models, show Δπ is structural\n697\t    not model-specific.\n698\t\n699\t    '\n700\t  expected_results:\n701\t    models_completed: 6\n702\t    effective_delta_pi_range: 0.08-0.198\n703\t    all_delta_pi_above_005: true\n704\t    worst_subgroup_consensus: True_medium (5/6 models)\n705\t    spearman_significant_pairs: 4\n706\t    filtered_subgroups: 4\n707\t    excluded_subgroups: False_long (n=6), True_long (n=4)\n708\t  result_rationale: 'Cross-model analysis 是 paper 的 supporting evidence——confirms\n709\t    the premise (heterogeneous  misclassification is structural) rather than validating\n710\t    the solution。All 6 models  Δπ>0.05 和 5/6 sharing worst subgroup 是 clean result。但\n711\t    Median reviewer notes： (1) Δπ range 0.08-0.198——the lower end (GPT-4o: 0.08, GPT-4.1:\n712\t    0.098) is moderate,  meaning most recent/best LLMs have modest heterogeneity where\n713\t    EC-HTE may not be needed  (K=2/moderate never crosses per exp-006)。(2) Only 4\n714\t    effective subgroups after filtering  (excluded n<10 groups)——limited statistical\n715\t    power for rank correlation (most p>0.20)。 (3) All OpenAI models——no open-source\n716\t    model diversity。Reviewer 将 exp-008 视为  \"nice supplement\" 放在 appendix appropriate，supports\n717\t    S6 (\"validates the premise\")  但不 move the needle on excitement。\n718\t\n719\t    '\n720\t  tables:\n721\t  - name: 'Table 14 (Appendix A): Effective Δπ Across LLMs'\n722\t    columns:\n723\t    - Model\n724\t    - Generation\n725\t    - Effective Δπ\n726\t    - Worst Subgroup\n727\t    - Overall Acc\n728\t    rows:\n729\t    - - gpt-3.5-turbo\n730\t      - '3.5'\n731\t      - '0.198'\n732\t      - True_medium\n733\t      - '0.72'\n734\t    - - gpt-4-turbo\n735\t      - '4'\n736\t      - '0.149'\n737\t      - True_medium\n738\t      - '0.81'\n739\t    - - gpt-4o\n740\t      - '4'\n741\t      - '0.080'\n742\t      - True_medium\n743\t      - '0.84'\n744\t    - - gpt-4o-mini\n745\t      - '4'\n746\t      - '0.136'\n747\t      - True_medium\n748\t      - '0.79'\n749\t    - - gpt-4.1\n750\t      - '4.1'\n751\t      - '0.098'\n752\t      - True_medium\n753\t      - '0.86'\n754\t    - - gpt-5.4\n755\t      - '5'\n756\t      - '0.114'\n757\t      - True_medium\n758\t      - '0.88'\n759\t  figures_description:\n760\t  - 'Appendix figure: bar chart of Δπ by model generation, showing heterogeneity persists\n761\t    but magnitude decreases with model capability.'\n762\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 接受 exp-008 的 premise validation 但注意到 paradox：better LLMs have\n763\t    lower Δπ， meaning the problem EC-HTE solves is becoming less severe as LLMs improve。GPT-5.4  Δπ=0.114\n764\t    vs GPT-3.5 Δπ=0.198——trend suggests the operating window is shrinking  over time。This\n765\t    doesn''t invalidate the paper but dampens enthusiasm for long-term  impact。Appendix\n766\t    placement appropriate。\n767\t\n768\t    '\n769\t- name: Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\n770\t  plan_id: exp-009\n771\t  description: 'CATE-weighted allocation targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups,\n772\t    compare against  uniform and uncertainty-only allocation strategies.\n773\t\n774\t    '\n775\t  expected_results:\n776\t    allocation_strategies: 3\n777\t    n_expert_total: 500\n778\t    K: 4\n779\t    cate_weighted_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform: 8-12%\n780\t    uncertainty_weighted_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform: 3-5%\n781\t    cate_weighted_coverage: 0.94\n782\t    uniform_coverage: 0.93\n783\t    practical_gain: modest\n784\t  result_rationale: 'Adaptive allocation 是 P2 experiment——appendix material。在 median\n785\t    tier 下 results  are positive but modest：8-12% RMSE improvement from CATE-weighted\n786\t    allocation vs  uniform。Reviewer 对此的反应是 \"interesting but tangential\"——allocation\n787\t    strategy  是 orthogonal to the core claims about bias identity and EC-HTE correction。Improvement  幅度不足以改变\n788\t    paper 的 overall narrative。Reviewer 可能 note that adaptive allocation  requires\n789\t    knowing which subgroups have high CATE and high error a priori——circular  if you\n790\t    don''t already have good subgroup estimates。不影响 overall score。\n791\t\n792\t    '\n793\t  tables:\n794\t  - name: 'Table 15 (Appendix B): Allocation Strategy Comparison'\n795\t    columns:\n796\t    - Strategy\n797\t    - RMSE\n798\t    - Coverage\n799\t    - '|Bias|'\n800\t    rows:\n801\t    - - Uniform\n802\t      - '0.108'\n803\t      - '0.93'\n804\t      - '0.012'\n805\t    - - Uncertainty-weighted\n806\t      - '0.103'\n807\t      - '0.93'\n808\t      - '0.011'\n809\t    - - CATE-weighted\n810\t      - '0.096'\n811\t      - '0.94'\n812\t      - '0.010'\n813\t  figures_description:\n814\t  - No figure; appendix table only.\n815\t  analysis: 'Appendix experiment，不影响 median tier scores。Reviewer 可能 skim 但 not cite\n816\t    in  review。Modest improvement (8-12%) 不足以成为 standalone contribution。在 revision  中可以\n817\t    strengthen 或 drop without affecting outcome。\n818\t\n819\t    '\n820\t- name: Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\n821\t  plan_id: exp-010\n822\t  description: 'Test EC-HTE when subgroups are noisy/overlapping (0%, 10%, 25%, 50%\n823\t    noise levels).  Show graceful degradation of HB partial pooling under misspecification.\n824\t\n825\t    '\n826\t  expected_results:\n827\t    noise_levels:\n828\t    - 0\n829\t    - 0.1\n830\t    - 0.25\n831\t    - 0.5\n832\t    total_runs: 800\n833\t    k2_coverage_hb_range: 0.945-0.958\n834\t    k2_coverage_naive_range: 0.875-0.897\n835\t    k2_coverage_global_range: 0.925-0.945\n836\t    k4_coverage_hb_range: 0.946-0.960\n837\t    hb_beats_mle_all_configs: true\n838\t    graceful_convergence_at_50pct: true\n839\t    hb_improvement_range: +0.1% to +0.9% RMSE\n840\t  result_rationale: 'Robustness analysis 是 positive result for paper——HB coverage\n841\t    维持 94.5-96% across all  noise levels，graceful convergence toward global at 50%\n842\t    noise。Reviewer 对 robustness  analysis 的 reaction：appreciate the thoroughness (supports\n843\t    S4 in review) 但 note that  improvement over MLE is very modest (+0.1% to +0.9%\n844\t    RMSE)。The real story is coverage  stability——naive drops to 87.5% while HB stays\n845\t    above 94.5%。但 reviewer also notes  that this experiment tests synthetic noise\n846\t    injection, not real-world subgroup  misspecification——real misspecification (wrong\n847\t    subgroup variable entirely) would be  more severe。Appendix material, supports\n848\t    robustness claim without changing scores。\n849\t\n850\t    '\n851\t  tables:\n852\t  - name: 'Table 16 (Appendix C): Coverage Under Subgroup Noise'\n853\t    columns:\n854\t    - Noise Level\n855\t    - K\n856\t    - Naive Cov\n857\t    - Global Cov\n858\t    - HB Cov\n859\t    rows:\n860\t    - - 0%\n861\t      - '2'\n862\t      - '0.875'\n863\t      - '0.925'\n864\t      - '0.958'\n865\t    - - 10%\n866\t      - '2'\n867\t      - '0.877'\n868\t      - '0.935'\n869\t      - '0.948'\n870\t    - - 25%\n871\t      - '2'\n872\t      - '0.890'\n873\t      - '0.932'\n874\t      - '0.950'\n875\t    - - 50%\n876\t      - '2'\n877\t      - '0.897'\n878\t      - '0.945'\n879\t      - '0.945'\n880\t    - - 0%\n881\t      - '4'\n882\t      - '0.904'\n883\t      - '0.930'\n884\t      - '0.956'\n885\t    - - 25%\n886\t      - '4'\n887\t      - '0.909'\n888\t      - '0.948'\n889\t      - '0.960'\n890\t    - - 50%\n891\t      - '4'\n892\t      - '0.919'\n893\t      - '0.944'\n894\t      - '0.946'\n895\t  figures_description:\n896\t  - No main text figure; coverage vs noise level line plot in appendix.\n897\t  analysis: 'Graceful degradation 是 expected result for HB shrinkage estimators——at\n898\t    maximum noise,  HB converges to global (by design)。Reviewer 不会对此 surprised 但 appreciate\n899\t    the  verification。Coverage as \"decisive metric\" 是 valid framing——naive 87-92%\n900\t    vs HB  95-96% is the strongest argument for EC-HTE in this experiment。但 improvement  is\n901\t    mainly in coverage (addressing undercoverage from ignoring heterogeneity), not  in\n902\t    point estimates。Supports Claim 2 at the margin。\n903\t\n904\t    '\n905\t- name: Causal Forest Integration\n906\t  plan_id: exp-011\n907\t  description: 'Apply EC-HTE post-hoc correction to CausalForestDML subgroup CATE\n908\t    estimates. Compare  naive, globally-corrected, and EC-HTE-corrected forests. K=2,4\n909\t    × extreme/moderate ×  n_expert=250,500.\n910\t\n911\t    '\n912\t  expected_results:\n913\t    n_mc: 100\n914\t    n_configs: 8\n915\t    total_rows: 144\n916\t    runtime_min: 35\n917\t    mean_abs_bias_naive_forest: 0.1558\n918\t    mean_abs_bias_global_forest: 0.1073\n919\t    mean_abs_bias_ec_hte_forest: 0.0608\n920\t    mean_rmse_naive_forest: 0.1782\n921\t    mean_rmse_global_forest: 0.1659\n922\t    mean_rmse_ec_hte_forest: 0.2289\n923\t    debiasing_hurts_cases: 9\n924\t    debiasing_hurts_max_ratio: 5.9\n925\t    k2_n500_ec_hte_bias_range: 0.004-0.013\n926\t    k2_n500_global_bias_range: 0.033-0.109\n927\t  result_rationale: 'CausalForest integration 是 paper 的 important validation——shows\n928\t    bias mechanism extends  beyond DIM to nonlinear CATE estimators，with amplification\n929\t    up to 5.9× (K=4/extreme)  vs 2.41× for DIM。EC-HTE achieves dramatic bias reduction\n930\t    (|bias|=0.06 vs naive 0.16,  62% reduction)。BUT the median-tier weakness is the\n931\t    RMSE tradeoff：EC-HTE RMSE 0.2289  is 38% HIGHER than global 0.1659。Reviewer W4\n932\t    (Moderate): \"EC-HTE reduces bias but  increases RMSE — by 38% for CausalForest.\n933\t    For practitioners, RMSE is often the primary  decision criterion.\" This experiment\n934\t    illustrates the fundamental bias-variance tradeoff  in EC-HTE：per-subgroup CM\n935\t    estimation reduces bias but introduces variance from small  expert samples。9 of\n936\t    144 rows show debiasing-hurts (global worse than naive)——confirms  Claim 1 generalizes\n937\t    to CausalForest。K=2/n=500 is the sweet spot: ec_hte |bias|=0.004-0.013  (near-zero)\n938\t    with manageable RMSE。But K=4/n=250 is the pain point：5.9× amplification  is dramatic\n939\t    但 EC-HTE RMSE penalty equally dramatic。\n940\t\n941\t    '\n942\t  tables:\n943\t  - name: 'Table 10: CausalForest Integration Results'\n944\t    columns:\n945\t    - Config\n946\t    - Method\n947\t    - '|Bias|'\n948\t    - RMSE\n949\t    - Coverage\n950\t    rows:\n951\t    - - K=2/extreme/n500\n952\t      - Naive CF\n953\t      - '0.125'\n954\t      - '0.143'\n955\t      - '0.46'\n956\t    - - K=2/extreme/n500\n957\t      - Global CF\n958\t      - '0.104'\n959\t      - '0.129'\n960\t      - '0.65'\n961\t    - - K=2/extreme/n500\n962\t      - EC-HTE CF\n963\t      - '0.008'\n964\t      - '0.082'\n965\t      - '0.91'\n966\t    - - K=4/extreme/n250\n967\t      - Naive CF\n968\t      - '0.186'\n969\t      - '0.202'\n970\t      - '0.42'\n971\t    - - K=4/extreme/n250\n972\t      - Global CF\n973\t      - '0.098'\n974\t      - '0.185'\n975\t      - '0.58'\n976\t    - - K=4/extreme/n250\n977\t      - EC-HTE CF\n978\t      - '0.042'\n979\t      - '0.285'\n980\t      - '0.88'\n981\t    - - Mean (all)\n982\t      - Naive CF\n983\t      - '0.156'\n984\t      - '0.178'\n985\t      - —\n986\t    - - Mean (all)\n987\t      - Global CF\n988\t      - '0.107'\n989\t      - '0.166'\n990\t      - —\n991\t    - - Mean (all)\n992\t      - EC-HTE CF\n993\t      - '0.061'\n994\t      - '0.229'\n995\t      - —\n996\t  figures_description:\n997\t  - Data contributes to bias mechanism schematic (Figure 1) showing DIM vs CausalForest\n998\t    amplification patterns.\n999\t  analysis: exp-011 的 dual signal 定义了 median tier 的 tension。Positive：5.9× amplification\n1000\t    with  CausalForest is the paper's most dramatic result，EC-HTE bias reduction to\n1001\t    near-zero  at K=2/n=500 is convincing。Negative：38% RMSE increase on average——reviewer\n1002\t    asks  \"would a practitioner accept 38% worse total estimation quality for lower\n1003\t    bias?\" The  answer depends on whether bias or RMSE is the relevant criterion，which\n1004\t    depends on  the downstream use case。Paper doesn't provide guidance on this choice。Reviewer\n1005\t    W4  requests \"explicit bias-RMSE Pareto analysis showing when EC-HTE actually\n1006\t    improves  total estimation quality versus when the variance cost outweighs the\n1007\t    bias reduction.\"  This is the key revision request connecting exp-011 to the overall\n1008\t    score。Coverage  improvement (naive 42-46% → EC-HTE 88-91%) is the strongest argument——undercoverage  leads\n1009\t    to false discoveries in downstream inference。\n1010\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ca06586-6e34-4743-9d58-fadda72796ca","uuid":"c45ecf4e-14c9-4501-be01-ccdd39e36ca5","timestamp":"2026-05-23T20:19:40.876Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260523T193110/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Problem framing 有吸引力但 novelty perception 分裂：部分 reviewer 认为 ''correction\n  can hurt''  是 known intuition 的 formalization，EC-HTE 的 narrow operating regime 削弱\n  practical impact， diagnostic 在 setting level 不 work。需要调整 claims 强度——Claim 1 降级为\n  ''first formal  characterization of classical ME amplification in LLM annotation\n  pipelines''，Claim 2 降级为  ''proof-of-concept correction demonstrating the identity\n  is actionable''，Claim 3 承认 diagnostic  仅在 subgroup level 有效。补充实验方向：找一个 EC-HTE 在\n  real data 上 works 的案例。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: 'Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE on synthetic data: HB Dirichlet-prior\n    confusion matrix estimator  with partial pooling, compare against MLE/Laplace\n    on full regime sweep (extreme/moderate/homogeneous  × n_expert 100-2000 × K=2,4\n    subgroups). 3600 MC runs.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mcmc_rhat_max: 1.024\n    mcmc_ess_min: 129\n    mcmc_divergent: 0\n    runtime_min: 69\n    total_mc_runs: 3600\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50: 4-9%\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n100: 1-2%\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate: 6-9%\n    hb_coverage_min: 0.87\n    hb_coverage_median: 0.93\n    k4_extreme_n50_hb_rmse: 0.99\n    hyperprior_sensitivity_k2_rmse_variation: <1%\n    hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_rmse_variation: ~4-5%\n    hyperprior_sensitivity_coverage_invariant: true\n  result_rationale: 'HB partial pooling 在 synthetic DGP 上 works as expected——这是 James-Stein\n    shrinkage 的 standard result，reviewer 不会对此感到 surprised。K=2 improvement 4-9% modest，K=4/extreme/n=50  曾出现\n    singularity blowup（修复后 RMSE 从 509→0.27），但 reviewer 会将此视为 implementation  issue\n    而非 fundamental limitation。Coverage 0.87-0.93 reasonable 但未达 nominal 0.95。 Median\n    reviewer 评价：technically sound (Soundness 3.5-4.0) 但 novelty 不高——HB Dirichlet  partial\n    pooling 是 established technique (Gelman et al. BDA3)，improvement 幅度 modest， 且\n    hyperprior sensitivity at K=4 (~4-5%) 暗示 method 对 specification 有一定 sensitivity。\n    这个实验支持 Claim 2 的 technical validity 但不足以让 reviewer 认为 method 有 substantial  practical\n    value。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=2)'\n    columns:\n    - n_expert\n    - Regime\n    - Subgroup\n    - MLE RMSE\n    - HB RMSE\n    - Δ%\n    rows:\n    - - '50'\n      - extreme\n      - z0\n      - '0.142'\n      - '0.131'\n      - -7.7%\n    - - '50'\n      - extreme\n      - z1\n      - '0.156'\n      - '0.142'\n      - -9.0%\n    - - '50'\n      - moderate\n      - z0\n      - '0.098'\n      - '0.094'\n      - -4.1%\n    - - '100'\n      - extreme\n      - z0\n      - '0.095'\n      - '0.093'\n      - -2.1%\n    - - '100'\n      - extreme\n      - z1\n      - '0.108'\n      - '0.107'\n      - -0.9%\n    - - '250'\n      - extreme\n      - z0\n      - '0.068'\n      - '0.067'\n      - -1.5%\n    - - '500'\n      - extreme\n      - z0\n      - '0.048'\n      - '0.048'\n      - -0.0%\n  - name: 'Table 4: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=4)'\n    columns:\n    - n_expert\n    - Regime\n    - Worst Subgroup\n    - MLE RMSE\n    - HB RMSE\n    - Δ%\n    rows:\n    - - '50'\n      - extreme\n      - D(π=0.30)\n      - '1.32'\n      - '0.99'\n      - -25.0%\n    - - '50'\n      - moderate\n      - C\n      - '0.186'\n      - '0.170'\n      - -8.6%\n    - - '100'\n      - extreme\n      - D(π=0.30)\n      - '0.38'\n      - '0.29'\n      - -23.7%\n    - - '250'\n      - extreme\n      - D\n      - '0.135'\n      - '0.128'\n      - -5.2%\n    - - '500'\n      - all\n      - all\n      - ~0.07\n      - ~0.07\n      - <0.5%\n  figures_description:\n  - No figures from this experiment in main text; data feeds into budget crossover\n    curves (Figure 4)\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 对 exp-001 的反应分两极：measurement error / causal inference 背景的 reviewer  认为\n    HB Dirichlet-Multinomial partial pooling 是 textbook technique（BDA3 Ch. 5）， improvement\n    仅 4-9%（K=2）到 25%（K=4/extreme worst-case），不构成 methodological  contribution。NLP\n    背景 reviewer 可能认为 3600 MC runs 的 thoroughness 是 strength。 Coverage 0.87-0.93 是\n    concern——未达 nominal 95%，reviewer 会问 why。Hyperprior  sensitivity at K=4 (~4-5%)\n    被视为 acceptable 但需要 disclosure。Overall：支持 soundness  score 3.5-4.0，但不显著提升 excitement。\n\n    '\n- name: Formal Bias Identity Verification\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: 'Derive bias = f(Δπ, Δτ) analytically, verify empirically across systematic\n    parameter grid.  Produce ''debiasing can hurt'' proposition with constructive\n    two-subgroup example. K>2 extension.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r2_k2: 0.9939\n    r2_k4: 0.9738\n    tightness_ratio_k2_median: 1.0027\n    tightness_ratio_k4_median: 1.0234\n    debiasing_hurts_pct: 50\n    debiasing_hurts_threshold_delta_misclass: 0.1235\n    max_bias_ratio_k2: 2.86\n    max_bias_ratio_k4: 2.41\n    coverage_2se_k2: 0.951\n    coverage_2se_k4: 0.94\n    total_configs: 520\n  result_rationale: 'R²>0.97 confirms the identity is exact at population level——finite-sample\n    MC noise 解释  remaining variance。这是 paper 最强的 technical result：product form Bias\n    ∝ Δπ×Δτ 是 exact  identity, not a bound。但 median reviewer 会有 novelty concern——至少一位\n    reviewer 有  measurement error / causal inference 背景，认为这是 Fuller (1987) / Carroll\n    (2006) 在 LLM  场景的 straightforward application。Qualitative insight \"correction\n    can hurt when error is  heterogeneous\" 是 known (Fuller 1987, Sec 2.3: \"misspecified\n    corrections amplify MSE\")。 Paper 的 contribution 是 (a) quantitative product form\n    和 (b) application to LLM annotation  pipelines。Debiasing hurts in 50% of parameter\n    space 是 striking 但需要 qualification—— 这 50% 包括所有 delta_misclass > 0.1235 的 configs，reviewer\n    问 \"how often does this  occur in practice?\"。Max amplification 2.86× (K=2) 和 2.41×\n    (K=4) 的 non-monotonic  K-dependence 是 nuanced result，但 reviewer 可能 view this as\n    \"moderate\" amplification  rather than \"dramatic\"。总体：claim1 被 75-90% reviewer 接受为\n    valid contribution，但  perceived novelty 被 downweight 到 2.5-3.5 因为 formal novelty\n    modest。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: Bias Identity Verification (R²)'\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - R²\n    - Tightness Ratio (median)\n    - Tightness Ratio (max)\n    rows:\n    - - '2'\n      - '0.994'\n      - '1.003'\n      - '1.021'\n    - - '4'\n      - '0.974'\n      - '1.023'\n      - '1.089'\n  - name: 'Table 2: Debiasing Hurts Analysis'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - K=2\n    - K=4\n    rows:\n    - - Configs where global hurts (%)\n      - 50%\n      - 50%\n    - - Max bias amplification (DIM)\n      - 2.86×\n      - 2.41×\n    - - Δπ threshold for hurt\n      - '0.124'\n      - '0.124'\n    - - Coverage (2SE)\n      - '0.951'\n      - '0.940'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2: Δπ × Δτ bias amplification heatmap — color intensity shows bias ratio\n    (global/naive), red region = debiasing hurts. Clear product-form structure visible.'\n  analysis: '这是 paper 的 theoretical backbone。Median reviewer 给 Soundness 3.5-4.0 因为\n    verification  thorough（520 configs, R²>0.97）。但 Excitement 因 novelty concern 被压到\n    3.0-3.5。 关键分歧点：NLP reviewer 可能认为 \"previously unrecognized bias mechanism\" 是 fair\n    claim； statistics reviewer 认为 qualitative insight is classical，quantitative form\n    只是  routine derivation in a new application context。Paper 需要 explicitly acknowledge  Fuller/Carroll\n    precedent 来 preempt 这个 objection（median framing 已 suggest  降级 claim wording）。50%\n    hurt rate 和 2.86× max amplification 虽然 noteworthy  但不足以让 skeptical reviewer 升\n    excitement score——需要 real-data demonstration  that this actually matters。\n\n    '\n- name: Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: 'Semi-synthetic benchmark using real CSS tweet corpus (TweetEval sentiment,\n    N=45K). Inject  known CATE heterogeneity structure, annotate with GPT-4.1, apply\n    EC-HTE vs baselines.  K=4 subgroups with misclass rates S0=0.05 to S3=0.25.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_subgroups: 4\n    misclass_rates: S0=0.05, S1=0.10, S2=0.15, S3=0.25\n    delta_pi: 0.2\n    debiasing_hurts_confirmed: true\n    mc_runs: 100\n    hb_vs_mle_n50_S3_extreme_rmse_change: -57% (HB worse)\n    hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme_rmse_change: +60% (HB dramatically better)\n    hb_vs_mle_n250_S3_rmse_change: +5-17% (HB better)\n    hb_crossover: n_expert=100 per subgroup\n    boundary_condition: n_expert>=100 recommended; n=50 with extreme heterogeneity\n      in tiny subgroups (12%) shows moderate degradation\n  result_rationale: 'Semi-synthetic 设计 validates the bias identity in a more realistic\n    setting——real text  corpus + injected CATE heterogeneity。Key finding: HB crossover\n    at ~n=100 per subgroup  (≥25 experts/subgroup for 12% minority subgroups)。Reviewer\n    接受 semi-synthetic 作为  valid evaluation framework 但注意到几个 concerns：(1) DGP 设计有 degrees\n    of freedom—— misclass rates S0=0.05 to S3=0.25 创造了 ideal conditions for EC-HTE\n    (Δπ=0.20 is \"extreme\")。 (2) n=50 boundary condition (HB worse by 57% at S3) 是\n    significant practical limitation—— K=4 with 12% minority means only 6 expert labels\n    per subgroup，too few for reliable CM  estimation。(3) Semi-synthetic 不能 fully substitute\n    for real-data validation。Reviewer  认为这个实验是 necessary but not sufficient for Claim\n    2。Pattern 与 exp-001 consistent， 支持 technical soundness。但 \"sweet spot is n=100-250\"\n    意味着 realistic expert budgets  are 400-1000 for K=4——reviewer 质疑 feasibility。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 5: Semi-Synthetic EC-HTE Performance (K=4, extreme)'\n    columns:\n    - n_expert\n    - Method\n    - Subgroup\n    - '|Bias|'\n    - RMSE\n    - Coverage\n    rows:\n    - - '50'\n      - Naive\n      - S3(π=0.25)\n      - '0.048'\n      - '0.109'\n      - '0.87'\n    - - '50'\n      - Global\n      - S3\n      - '0.110'\n      - '0.140'\n      - '0.92'\n    - - '50'\n      - MLE\n      - S3\n      - '0.085'\n      - '0.280'\n      - '0.90'\n    - - '50'\n      - HB\n      - S3\n      - '0.072'\n      - '0.292'\n      - '0.93'\n    - - '100'\n      - HB\n      - S3\n      - '0.018'\n      - '0.112'\n      - '0.94'\n    - - '100'\n      - Global\n      - S3\n      - '0.105'\n      - '0.138'\n      - '0.92'\n    - - '250'\n      - HB\n      - S3\n      - '0.009'\n      - '0.074'\n      - '0.95'\n    - - '500'\n      - HB\n      - all avg\n      - '0.005'\n      - '0.052'\n      - '0.95'\n  figures_description:\n  - Data feeds into Figure 4 (budget crossover curves)\n  analysis: 'Semi-synthetic 是 most controlled validation——reviewer 认为 technically\n    sound 但 asks  \"how representative is this DGP?\" Δπ=0.20 是 extreme regime，而 exp-012\n    pilot 显示  real GPT-4.1 的 Δπ=0.098 only (moderate)。这暗示 paper 的 headline numbers\n    (near-zero  bias at n=250) 对应的是 favorable conditions，real-world performance 会\n    worse。Claim 2  accepted as useful by 40-60%：technical validity 无争议，但 practical\n    utility window  被认为 narrow。\n\n    '\n- name: Real-Data Case Study (Pattern Consistency)\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 'Apply EC-HTE to UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech corpus (N=2496).\n    Show pattern consistency  with synthetic results. Framed as illustrative application,\n    NOT ground-truth benchmark.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dataset: UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\n    n_comments: 2496\n    subgroups: 4\n    delta_pi: 0.117\n    global_FPR: 0.139\n    global_FNR: 0.533\n    avg_abs_bias_naive: 0.21\n    avg_abs_bias_global: 0.273\n    avg_abs_bias_ec_hte: 0.313\n    ec_hte_outperforms_global: false\n    cate_comparison: EC-HTE does not outperform global — high FNR (53%) and wide CIs\n      limit correction effectiveness\n  result_rationale: '这是 median tier 的 critical weakness。EC-HTE avg |bias| 0.313 >\n    global 0.273 > naive 0.210  ——method 在 real data 上 makes things worse。Root cause：(1)\n    global FNR=0.533 (LLM 严重  under-classifies dehumanization)，近乎 random for positive\n    class，CM inversion amplifies  noise；(2) Δπ=0.117 is moderate, not extreme；(3)\n    subgroup-level expert labels insufficient。 Paper 将此 frame 为 \"operating condition\n    mismatch\" 和 \"illustrative application\"，但  reviewer 的反应是：这恰好是 the kind of real-world\n    setting where practitioners would  apply the method。如果 method 仅在 carefully controlled\n    synthetic conditions 下 work， practical impact 严重受限。至少一位 reviewer 将此视为 major weakness，directly\n    影响  Claim 2 acceptance rate (40-60%) 和 overall excitement (3.0-3.5)。Honest reporting  被\n    appreciated (S3 in review) 但不 mitigate the fundamental concern。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 12: Real-Data Case Study — UC Berkeley Hate Speech'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Avg |Bias|\n    - Subgroup Max |Bias|\n    - Mean CI Width\n    rows:\n    - - Naive\n      - '0.210'\n      - '0.35'\n      - '0.18'\n    - - Global Corrected\n      - '0.273'\n      - '0.42'\n      - '0.22'\n    - - EC-HTE (HB)\n      - '0.313'\n      - '0.51'\n      - '0.34'\n  - name: 'Table 13: Subgroup Misclassification Rates'\n    columns:\n    - Subgroup\n    - FPR\n    - FNR\n    - Overall Error\n    - n\n    rows:\n    - - plat0_long\n      - '0.064'\n      - '0.468'\n      - '0.266'\n      - '624'\n    - - plat0_short\n      - '0.101'\n      - '0.573'\n      - '0.337'\n      - '624'\n    - - plat23_long\n      - '0.077'\n      - '0.530'\n      - '0.303'\n      - '624'\n    - - plat23_short\n      - '0.139'\n      - '0.627'\n      - '0.383'\n      - '624'\n  figures_description:\n  - No figure; results presented as tables only. Reviewer W5 notes absence of figures\n    as presentation weakness.\n  analysis: 'exp-004 是 median tier 最被 reviewer 攻击的实验。W2 (Major) in review: \"EC-HTE''s\n    average  absolute bias (0.313) is worse than both naive (0.210) and global corrected\n    (0.273).\"  Paper 的 defense (\"operating condition mismatch\") 在逻辑上成立（FNR=53% violates  practical\n    CM invertibility），但 reviewer 反问：\"how often do real datasets satisfy  the conditions?\"\n    这直接压低 Claim 2 acceptance 到 40-60%。exp-015/016 的 negative  results 进一步 confirm：neither\n    low-FNR (gpt-3.5) nor low-FPR (GPT-4.1) real CMs  enable EC-HTE to beat global\n    when P(Z=1)=0.18。Median reviewer 接受 honest disclosure  但给 excitement 3.0——\"the\n    method fails outside carefully controlled synthetic conditions.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Diagnostic Criterion Validation\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Compute Δπ × Δτ product from pilot data across all settings. ROC analysis\n    of threshold  for predicting when global correction fails. Cross-validated evaluation.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    subgroup_level_auc: 0.833\n    subgroup_level_correlation: 0.86\n    setting_level_auc: 0.49\n    low_pi_hurt_pct: 84.6\n    high_pi_hurt_pct: 15.4\n    theory_alignment: consistent with exp-002 formula\n  result_rationale: 'Setting-level AUC=0.49 是 median tier 的 second critical weakness。Diagnostic\n    在 practitioner  实际需要做决策的 granularity（\"should I use EC-HTE for this analysis?\"）上\n    no better than  random。Subgroup-level AUC=0.833 表面上 impressive，但 reviewer 指出两个问题：(1)\n    subgroup-level  decision 需要已知 subgroup structure，而 knowing which subgroups exist\n    本身就需要 domain  knowledge——循环论证；(2) AUC 0.833 with ~15% false positive rate means\n    1 in 7 flagged  subgroups is false alarm。Claim 3 accepted by only 30-50% of reviewers。Paper\n    的 reframe  (\"two-stage decision workflow: flag subgroups → consult budget\") partially\n    mitigates but  doesn''t resolve the fundamental gap。Reviewer 建议 explore alternative\n    diagnostic statistics  or acknowledge diagnostic is subgroup-level only。This experiment\n    直接决定了 Claim 3 的 fate  in median tier。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 11: Diagnostic Criterion Performance'\n    columns:\n    - Level\n    - AUC\n    - Correlation\n    - Precision@0.5\n    - Recall@0.5\n    rows:\n    - - Subgroup-level\n      - '0.833'\n      - '0.86'\n      - '0.78'\n      - '0.85'\n    - - Setting-level (CV)\n      - '0.49'\n      - '0.12'\n      - '0.51'\n      - '0.48'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 3: Subgroup-level ROC curve for Δπ×Δτ diagnostic. Shows reasonable discrimination\n    at subgroup level (AUC=0.83) but would need separate panel showing setting-level\n    failure (AUC=0.49) for honest presentation.'\n  analysis: 'exp-005 的 split result 是 median tier 的 defining feature。Strong subgroup\n    AUC + failed  setting AUC creates a narrative tension：the diagnostic works where\n    you already know the  answer (subgroup level) but fails where you need it most\n    (setting level)。Reviewer W1 (Major):  \"Contribution 3 in the introduction leads\n    with ''AUC=0.83'' without immediately clarifying  this is subgroup-level only\n    — this creates a misleading first impression.\" Paper 需要  reframe Claim 3 更 carefully——lead\n    with setting-level failure, then present subgroup-level  as partial recovery。This\n    is the key revision request for median tier.\n\n    '\n- name: Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 'Systematic sweep n_expert ∈ {50, 100, 250, 500, 1000, 2000} × K ∈\n    {2, 4} × regime.  Find crossover point where EC-HTE > Global on RMSE. Validate\n    HB partial pooling value.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_rows: 288\n    runtime_min: 110\n    crossover_K2_extreme: 250\n    crossover_K2_moderate: never\n    crossover_K4_extreme: 1000\n    crossover_K4_moderate: 2000\n    hb_vs_mle_win_rate: 21/24 (87.5%)\n    hb_best_improvement_over_mle: +42.4% RMSE at K4/moderate/n50\n    convergence_at_n1000: <0.5% HB-MLE difference\n    rmse_penalty_k4_n50: up to 4.9×\n    rmse_penalty_k4_n100: up to 3.5×\n  result_rationale: 'Budget sweep 是 double-edged sword for median tier。Positive：provides\n    precise, actionable  crossover thresholds——reviewer 认为 this is good science。Negative：reveals\n    that EC-HTE  operating window is restrictive。K=2/moderate: EC-HTE NEVER outperforms\n    global on RMSE。 K=4/extreme: crossover at n=1000 (= 250 experts per subgroup)——expensive。K=4/moderate:  crossover\n    at n=2000——impractical for most CSS studies。RMSE penalties at small n (up to  4.9×)\n    被 reviewer 视为 \"significant practical limitation, not just honest disclosure\"  (median\n    core assumption #5)。W3 (Major) in review: \"the practical applicability window\n    is  narrower than the paper''s framing suggests.\" 这个实验 honest 但 directly undermines  excitement：reviewer\n    计算 \"for a typical CSS study with K=4 subgroups and moderate  heterogeneity, I\n    need 2000 expert labels — that''s a large-scale annotation project,  not a quick\n    pilot.\" Abstract 的 \"as few as 250 expert labels\" technically correct  (K=2/extreme)\n    but cherry-picks the best case。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 6: RMSE Crossover Points'\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - Regime\n    - n_expert crossover\n    - Practical?\n    rows:\n    - - '2'\n      - extreme\n      - '250'\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - '2'\n      - moderate\n      - never\n      - N/A — global always better\n    - - '4'\n      - extreme\n      - '1000'\n      - Marginal\n    - - '4'\n      - moderate\n      - '2000'\n      - Expensive\n  - name: 'Table 7: RMSE Penalty at Small n_expert'\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - n_expert\n    - RMSE ratio (EC-HTE / Global)\n    - Worst subgroup\n    rows:\n    - - '2'\n      - '50'\n      - 1.8×\n      - z1\n    - - '4'\n      - '50'\n      - 4.9×\n      - D(π=0.30)\n    - - '4'\n      - '100'\n      - 3.5×\n      - D\n    - - '4'\n      - '250'\n      - 1.4×\n      - D\n    - - '4'\n      - '500'\n      - 1.1×\n      - all comparable\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 4: Budget crossover curves — RMSE ratio (EC-HTE/Global) vs n_expert for\n    each (K, regime) combination. Shows EC-HTE only wins at large n for extreme heterogeneity.'\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 对 exp-006 的反应：appreciate the thoroughness but use the data against\n    Claim 2。 \"EC-HTE is most valuable precisely when it is most needed\" 的 narrative\n    被 reviewer  接受 in principle，但 \"most needed\" (extreme heterogeneity) 和 \"affordable\"\n    (n≤250)  的交集太小。W3 highlights that K=2/moderate NEVER crosses——meaning for the\n    majority  of real-world scenarios (moderate heterogeneity is more common than\n    extreme), global  correction is the right choice。This 是 Claim 2 acceptance rate\n    被压到 40-60% 的 key  evidence。Paper 的 defense 是 connecting to Claim 3 (diagnostic\n    decides strategy)， 但 Claim 3 itself 在 setting level 不 work (exp-005)，所以 the chain\n    breaks。\n\n    '\n- name: PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: '(a) PPCI vs EC-HTE on covariate vs outcome error; (b) per-subgroup\n    DSL baseline;  (c) EC-HTE+PPCI composition for dual error; (d) pure covariate-error\n    control condition.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_rows: 6912\n    dgps:\n    - A_covariate_only\n    - B_outcome_only\n    - C_both_errors\n    - D_no_error\n    methods: 8\n    mc_runs: 100\n    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias: 0.005\n    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_ppci_rmse: 0.225\n    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ec_hte_bias: 0.178\n    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_bias: 0.004\n    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2_ppci_rmse: 0.261\n    dgp_c_n500_k2_ec_hte_ppci_bias: 0.005\n    dgp_c_n500_k2_ec_hte_ppci_rmse: 0.142\n    composition_bias_reduction_over_echte: 35×\n    coverage_all_ppci_methods: 1.0\n  result_rationale: 'PPCI composition 是 paper 的 technical highlight——35× bias reduction\n    in DGP C，near-zero  bias (0.005)。Median reviewer 对 composition result positive\n    但有两个 qualifications： (1) PPCI alone (bias=0.004) achieves similar bias reduction\n    in DGP C without EC-HTE— reviewer 问 \"is EC-HTE really necessary here?\"。Paper 的\n    answer 是 PPCI has higher  RMSE (0.261 vs 0.225) 和 doesn''t exploit CM structure——technically\n    correct but the  advantage is modest。(2) Coverage=1.0 for all PPCI methods (W8\n    in review): \"Perfect  empirical coverage across 100 MC runs is statistically improbable\n    under correct  calibration — this likely reflects inflated CIs.\" Over-conservative\n    CIs 意味着 PPCI  methods 的 precision 很差。Reviewer 对 DSL comparison 接受——EC-HTE 的 partial\n    pooling  advantage over per-subgroup DSL 是 valid。Overall：composition elevates\n    Claim 4 但  doesn''t rescue Claims 2-3。DGP A (pure covariate error) 是 EC-HTE 的\n    strength case， reviewer 认可。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8: DGP C (Both Errors) — Key Results'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - '|Bias| (z0)'\n    - RMSE (z0)\n    - Coverage\n    rows:\n    - - Naive\n      - '0.251'\n      - '0.269'\n      - '0.85'\n    - - Global CM\n      - '0.195'\n      - '0.238'\n      - '0.88'\n    - - EC-HTE\n      - '0.178'\n      - '0.226'\n      - '0.92'\n    - - PPCI\n      - '0.004'\n      - '0.261'\n      - '1.00'\n    - - EC-HTE+PPCI\n      - '0.005'\n      - '0.225'\n      - '1.00'\n    - - Oracle (cov)\n      - '0.180'\n      - '0.215'\n      - '0.93'\n  - name: 'Table 9: Cross-DGP Method Comparison (n=250, K=2, extreme)'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - DGP A |Bias|\n    - DGP B |Bias|\n    - DGP C |Bias|\n    - DGP D |Bias|\n    rows:\n    - - Naive\n      - '0.12'\n      - '0.14'\n      - '0.25'\n      - '0.001'\n    - - Global\n      - '0.08'\n      - '0.09'\n      - '0.20'\n      - '0.001'\n    - - EC-HTE\n      - '0.01'\n      - '0.13'\n      - '0.18'\n      - '0.001'\n    - - PPCI\n      - '0.03'\n      - '0.01'\n      - '0.004'\n      - '0.001'\n    - - EC-HTE+PPCI\n      - '0.01'\n      - '0.01'\n      - '0.005'\n      - '0.001'\n  figures_description:\n  - Data presented in tables; no dedicated figure. Could benefit from a DGP comparison\n    bar chart.\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 对 PPCI composition 的评价：S5 (\"principled and effective\") 但视为 secondary  contribution。Key\n    tension：在 DGP C 中 PPCI alone (bias=0.004) 几乎与 EC-HTE+PPCI  (0.005) 一样好——EC-HTE\n    的 marginal value 主要在 RMSE (0.261→0.225, 14% improvement)。 Reviewer 不认为这足以 justify\n    EC-HTE 的 complexity。Coverage=1.0 被视为 red flag  (over-conservative CIs)——Q4 in\n    review 直接问 CI width。This experiment supports  soundness 3.5-4.0 but contributes\n    modestly to excitement。\n\n    '\n- name: Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: 'GPT-3.5-turbo through GPT-5.4 (6 models, three generations): measure\n    misclassification  heterogeneity patterns across models, show Δπ is structural\n    not model-specific.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    models_completed: 6\n    effective_delta_pi_range: 0.08-0.198\n    all_delta_pi_above_005: true\n    worst_subgroup_consensus: True_medium (5/6 models)\n    spearman_significant_pairs: 4\n    filtered_subgroups: 4\n    excluded_subgroups: False_long (n=6), True_long (n=4)\n  result_rationale: 'Cross-model analysis 是 paper 的 supporting evidence——confirms\n    the premise (heterogeneous  misclassification is structural) rather than validating\n    the solution。All 6 models  Δπ>0.05 和 5/6 sharing worst subgroup 是 clean result。但\n    Median reviewer notes： (1) Δπ range 0.08-0.198——the lower end (GPT-4o: 0.08, GPT-4.1:\n    0.098) is moderate,  meaning most recent/best LLMs have modest heterogeneity where\n    EC-HTE may not be needed  (K=2/moderate never crosses per exp-006)。(2) Only 4\n    effective subgroups after filtering  (excluded n<10 groups)——limited statistical\n    power for rank correlation (most p>0.20)。 (3) All OpenAI models——no open-source\n    model diversity。Reviewer 将 exp-008 视为  \"nice supplement\" 放在 appendix appropriate，supports\n    S6 (\"validates the premise\")  但不 move the needle on excitement。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 14 (Appendix A): Effective Δπ Across LLMs'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Generation\n    - Effective Δπ\n    - Worst Subgroup\n    - Overall Acc\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-3.5-turbo\n      - '3.5'\n      - '0.198'\n      - True_medium\n      - '0.72'\n    - - gpt-4-turbo\n      - '4'\n      - '0.149'\n      - True_medium\n      - '0.81'\n    - - gpt-4o\n      - '4'\n      - '0.080'\n      - True_medium\n      - '0.84'\n    - - gpt-4o-mini\n      - '4'\n      - '0.136'\n      - True_medium\n      - '0.79'\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - '4.1'\n      - '0.098'\n      - True_medium\n      - '0.86'\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - '5'\n      - '0.114'\n      - True_medium\n      - '0.88'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Appendix figure: bar chart of Δπ by model generation, showing heterogeneity persists\n    but magnitude decreases with model capability.'\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 接受 exp-008 的 premise validation 但注意到 paradox：better LLMs have\n    lower Δπ， meaning the problem EC-HTE solves is becoming less severe as LLMs improve。GPT-5.4  Δπ=0.114\n    vs GPT-3.5 Δπ=0.198——trend suggests the operating window is shrinking  over time。This\n    doesn''t invalidate the paper but dampens enthusiasm for long-term  impact。Appendix\n    placement appropriate。\n\n    '\n- name: Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 'CATE-weighted allocation targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups,\n    compare against  uniform and uncertainty-only allocation strategies.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    allocation_strategies: 3\n    n_expert_total: 500\n    K: 4\n    cate_weighted_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform: 8-12%\n    uncertainty_weighted_rmse_improvement_vs_uniform: 3-5%\n    cate_weighted_coverage: 0.94\n    uniform_coverage: 0.93\n    practical_gain: modest\n  result_rationale: 'Adaptive allocation 是 P2 experiment——appendix material。在 median\n    tier 下 results  are positive but modest：8-12% RMSE improvement from CATE-weighted\n    allocation vs  uniform。Reviewer 对此的反应是 \"interesting but tangential\"——allocation\n    strategy  是 orthogonal to the core claims about bias identity and EC-HTE correction。Improvement  幅度不足以改变\n    paper 的 overall narrative。Reviewer 可能 note that adaptive allocation  requires\n    knowing which subgroups have high CATE and high error a priori——circular  if you\n    don''t already have good subgroup estimates。不影响 overall score。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 15 (Appendix B): Allocation Strategy Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Strategy\n    - RMSE\n    - Coverage\n    - '|Bias|'\n    rows:\n    - - Uniform\n      - '0.108'\n      - '0.93'\n      - '0.012'\n    - - Uncertainty-weighted\n      - '0.103'\n      - '0.93'\n      - '0.011'\n    - - CATE-weighted\n      - '0.096'\n      - '0.94'\n      - '0.010'\n  figures_description:\n  - No figure; appendix table only.\n  analysis: 'Appendix experiment，不影响 median tier scores。Reviewer 可能 skim 但 not cite\n    in  review。Modest improvement (8-12%) 不足以成为 standalone contribution。在 revision  中可以\n    strengthen 或 drop without affecting outcome。\n\n    '\n- name: Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: 'Test EC-HTE when subgroups are noisy/overlapping (0%, 10%, 25%, 50%\n    noise levels).  Show graceful degradation of HB partial pooling under misspecification.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    noise_levels:\n    - 0\n    - 0.1\n    - 0.25\n    - 0.5\n    total_runs: 800\n    k2_coverage_hb_range: 0.945-0.958\n    k2_coverage_naive_range: 0.875-0.897\n    k2_coverage_global_range: 0.925-0.945\n    k4_coverage_hb_range: 0.946-0.960\n    hb_beats_mle_all_configs: true\n    graceful_convergence_at_50pct: true\n    hb_improvement_range: +0.1% to +0.9% RMSE\n  result_rationale: 'Robustness analysis 是 positive result for paper——HB coverage\n    维持 94.5-96% across all  noise levels，graceful convergence toward global at 50%\n    noise。Reviewer 对 robustness  analysis 的 reaction：appreciate the thoroughness (supports\n    S4 in review) 但 note that  improvement over MLE is very modest (+0.1% to +0.9%\n    RMSE)。The real story is coverage  stability——naive drops to 87.5% while HB stays\n    above 94.5%。但 reviewer also notes  that this experiment tests synthetic noise\n    injection, not real-world subgroup  misspecification——real misspecification (wrong\n    subgroup variable entirely) would be  more severe。Appendix material, supports\n    robustness claim without changing scores。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 16 (Appendix C): Coverage Under Subgroup Noise'\n    columns:\n    - Noise Level\n    - K\n    - Naive Cov\n    - Global Cov\n    - HB Cov\n    rows:\n    - - 0%\n      - '2'\n      - '0.875'\n      - '0.925'\n      - '0.958'\n    - - 10%\n      - '2'\n      - '0.877'\n      - '0.935'\n      - '0.948'\n    - - 25%\n      - '2'\n      - '0.890'\n      - '0.932'\n      - '0.950'\n    - - 50%\n      - '2'\n      - '0.897'\n      - '0.945'\n      - '0.945'\n    - - 0%\n      - '4'\n      - '0.904'\n      - '0.930'\n      - '0.956'\n    - - 25%\n      - '4'\n      - '0.909'\n      - '0.948'\n      - '0.960'\n    - - 50%\n      - '4'\n      - '0.919'\n      - '0.944'\n      - '0.946'\n  figures_description:\n  - No main text figure; coverage vs noise level line plot in appendix.\n  analysis: 'Graceful degradation 是 expected result for HB shrinkage estimators——at\n    maximum noise,  HB converges to global (by design)。Reviewer 不会对此 surprised 但 appreciate\n    the  verification。Coverage as \"decisive metric\" 是 valid framing——naive 87-92%\n    vs HB  95-96% is the strongest argument for EC-HTE in this experiment。但 improvement  is\n    mainly in coverage (addressing undercoverage from ignoring heterogeneity), not  in\n    point estimates。Supports Claim 2 at the margin。\n\n    '\n- name: Causal Forest Integration\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 'Apply EC-HTE post-hoc correction to CausalForestDML subgroup CATE\n    estimates. Compare  naive, globally-corrected, and EC-HTE-corrected forests. K=2,4\n    × extreme/moderate ×  n_expert=250,500.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_mc: 100\n    n_configs: 8\n    total_rows: 144\n    runtime_min: 35\n    mean_abs_bias_naive_forest: 0.1558\n    mean_abs_bias_global_forest: 0.1073\n    mean_abs_bias_ec_hte_forest: 0.0608\n    mean_rmse_naive_forest: 0.1782\n    mean_rmse_global_forest: 0.1659\n    mean_rmse_ec_hte_forest: 0.2289\n    debiasing_hurts_cases: 9\n    debiasing_hurts_max_ratio: 5.9\n    k2_n500_ec_hte_bias_range: 0.004-0.013\n    k2_n500_global_bias_range: 0.033-0.109\n  result_rationale: 'CausalForest integration 是 paper 的 important validation——shows\n    bias mechanism extends  beyond DIM to nonlinear CATE estimators，with amplification\n    up to 5.9× (K=4/extreme)  vs 2.41× for DIM。EC-HTE achieves dramatic bias reduction\n    (|bias|=0.06 vs naive 0.16,  62% reduction)。BUT the median-tier weakness is the\n    RMSE tradeoff：EC-HTE RMSE 0.2289  is 38% HIGHER than global 0.1659。Reviewer W4\n    (Moderate): \"EC-HTE reduces bias but  increases RMSE — by 38% for CausalForest.\n    For practitioners, RMSE is often the primary  decision criterion.\" This experiment\n    illustrates the fundamental bias-variance tradeoff  in EC-HTE：per-subgroup CM\n    estimation reduces bias but introduces variance from small  expert samples。9 of\n    144 rows show debiasing-hurts (global worse than naive)——confirms  Claim 1 generalizes\n    to CausalForest。K=2/n=500 is the sweet spot: ec_hte |bias|=0.004-0.013  (near-zero)\n    with manageable RMSE。But K=4/n=250 is the pain point：5.9× amplification  is dramatic\n    但 EC-HTE RMSE penalty equally dramatic。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 10: CausalForest Integration Results'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - Method\n    - '|Bias|'\n    - RMSE\n    - Coverage\n    rows:\n    - - K=2/extreme/n500\n      - Naive CF\n      - '0.125'\n      - '0.143'\n      - '0.46'\n    - - K=2/extreme/n500\n      - Global CF\n      - '0.104'\n      - '0.129'\n      - '0.65'\n    - - K=2/extreme/n500\n      - EC-HTE CF\n      - '0.008'\n      - '0.082'\n      - '0.91'\n    - - K=4/extreme/n250\n      - Naive CF\n      - '0.186'\n      - '0.202'\n      - '0.42'\n    - - K=4/extreme/n250\n      - Global CF\n      - '0.098'\n      - '0.185'\n      - '0.58'\n    - - K=4/extreme/n250\n      - EC-HTE CF\n      - '0.042'\n      - '0.285'\n      - '0.88'\n    - - Mean (all)\n      - Naive CF\n      - '0.156'\n      - '0.178'\n      - —\n    - - Mean (all)\n      - Global CF\n      - '0.107'\n      - '0.166'\n      - —\n    - - Mean (all)\n      - EC-HTE CF\n      - '0.061'\n      - '0.229'\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - Data contributes to bias mechanism schematic (Figure 1) showing DIM vs CausalForest\n    amplification patterns.\n  analysis: exp-011 的 dual signal 定义了 median tier 的 tension。Positive：5.9× amplification\n    with  CausalForest is the paper's most dramatic result，EC-HTE bias reduction to\n    near-zero  at K=2/n=500 is convincing。Negative：38% RMSE increase on average——reviewer\n    asks  \"would a practitioner accept 38% worse total estimation quality for lower\n    bias?\" The  answer depends on whether bias or RMSE is the relevant criterion，which\n    depends on  the downstream use case。Paper doesn't provide guidance on this choice。Reviewer\n    W4  requests \"explicit bias-RMSE Pareto analysis showing when EC-HTE actually\n    improves  total estimation quality versus when the variance cost outweighs the\n    bias reduction.\"  This is the key revision request connecting exp-011 to the overall\n    score。Coverage  improvement (naive 42-46% → EC-HTE 88-91%) is the strongest argument——undercoverage  leads\n    to false discoveries in downstream inference。\n","numLines":1010,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1010}}}
